  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the files needed to investigate and reproduce this bug:\n\n1. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py`** \u2014 root cause. Contains `install_artifact()`, which builds the custom normalized-name cache via `{m.name.removesuffix(os.path.sep): m for m in collection_tar.getmembers()}` (with the comment `# Workaround for https://bugs.python.org/issue47231`), plus `_extract_tar_dir()` and `_get_tar_file_member()`, which consume that cache during extraction.\n2. **`test/units/galaxy/test_collection.py`** \u2014 existing unit tests for this exact module; shows established patterns for constructing in-memory `tarfile` objects and members to model a regression test after.\n3. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/concrete_artifact_manager.py`** \u2014 shows the \"correct\" pattern (`collection_tar.getmember(MANIFEST_FILENAME)` using the standard API directly), useful contrast for demonstrating what the fix should look like.\n4. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/role.py`** \u2014 references the same underlying CPython tarfile issue in a comment, useful corroborating context for the workaround's origin/justification.\n5. **`test/units/cli/test_galaxy.py`** \u2014 another existing test file exercising `tar.getmembers()` against galaxy collection tarballs, useful as a secondary fixture-construction reference.",
